# P2P API testing

## 1. Oracle

`docs/API.md` and `/openapi.json` define correct behavior. If the running API differs, keep the documented expectation and let the test fail — report the defect; never weaken or rewrite the assertion to match the API. Behavior neither document covers belongs in `docs/QUESTIONS.md` as assumed until a human answers; do not assert it yet.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — docs say inactive vendor → 400 inactive_vendor_gate
const res = await request.post('/purchase-orders', {
  data: { vendor_id: 'vnd-002', line_items: [{ sku: 'LUM-2X4-8', quantity: 10, unit_price: 4.75 }] },
});
expect(res.status()).toBe(400);
expect((await res.json()).rule).toBe('inactive_vendor_gate');

// ❌ BAD — API returned 201, so the test “passes” with wrong expectations
expect([201, 400]).toContain(res.status());
```

## 2. Black box

Tests call HTTP only. Never import, read, or change anything under `src/`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const res = await request.get('/vendors');

// ❌ BAD
import { store } from '../../src/store';
```

## 3. Requests

Use Playwright’s `request` fixture with path-only URLs; host and port come from `baseURL` in `playwright.config.ts` (`API_BASE_URL`).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
await request.get('/health');

// ❌ BAD
await request.get('http://localhost:8000/vendors');
```

## 4. Data

Each test creates what it needs: own vendor for exposure checks, unique `invoice_number` values (e.g. `` `INV-${Date.now()}` ``). Never call `POST /admin/reset` inside a test — only `tests/api/reset.setup.ts` does that before the run. Do not rely on another test’s records except steps in one serial `@e2e` flow.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const vendor = await request.post('/vendors', { data: { name: `QA ${Date.now()}` } });
const invoiceNumber = `INV-${Date.now()}`;

// ❌ BAD — assumes seed PO from a prior test file
await request.post('/invoices', { data: { po_id: 'po-from-other-spec', invoice_number: 'INV-1', line_items: [...] } });
```

## 5. Per endpoint

Cover each endpoint with three cases: **positive** (happy path), **negative** (one invalid input or one rule violation at a time → 400 with `validation_error` or the named rule), **error** (unknown id → 404).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — POST /vendors: 201, empty name → 400 validation_error, GET exposure unknown → 404

// ❌ BAD — only GET /vendors 200, no POST negative or exposure 404
```

## 6. Assertions

Assert status; on every 400 assert the exact `rule` (wrong rule = fail). Assert values that matter (`open_ap_liability`, `ordered_value`, `partial_receipt`), not merely that a key exists. Validate response shape with `expectSchema` against OpenAPI component schemas (P48).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
expect(body.rule).toBe('receive_quantity_limit');
expect(body.open_ap_liability).toBe(95.1);
await expectSchema(body, 'VendorExposure');

// ❌ BAD
expect(body).toHaveProperty('rule');
expect(res.status()).toBe(400); // no rule check
```

## 7. Tags

Exactly one tag per test: `{ tag: '@api' }` for a single endpoint, `{ tag: '@e2e' }` for a multi-step flow. Put the tag on `test()`, never on `describe()`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
test('POST /purchase-orders rejects inactive vendor', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ request }) => { ... });

// ❌ BAD
test.describe('vendors', { tag: '@api' }, () => { ... });
```

## 8. Known bugs

A test for a confirmed bug keeps full assertions and uses `test.fail(true, 'BUG-<n>: <one line>')`. Never delete the test or loosen expectations.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
test('duplicate invoice detection is case-insensitive', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ request }) => {
  test.fail(true, 'BUG-3: second INV-7 accepted with 201');
  // ... full documented expectations ...
});

// ❌ BAD — bug “fixed” in the test by expecting 201
expect(second.status()).toBe(201);
```

## 9. Evidence

Label every behavioral claim in comments, reports, or `docs/QUESTIONS.md`: **executed** (this run proved it), **inspected only** (read from docs/OpenAPI, not exercised), or **not yet tested**.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
- inactive_vendor_gate on vnd-002 → 400 — executed
- Empty PO line_items rejected — not yet tested

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
- All 11 rules are covered (no label, no proof)
```
